PE 807: Rododdle / 杆旋转

=== Problem Description ===
Given N rods of various lengths placed on a line,
each rod can rotate 180 degrees around its center.
The goal is to minimize the total length of the convex hull
or envelope of the rod endpoints.

=== Small Example ===
Consider 2 rods of lengths 3 and 4:
  Both horizontal: extension = 3 + 4 = 7
  Both vertical: envelope = sqrt(3^2 + 4^2) = 5 (if aligned)
  Different orientations change the bounding box.

=== Problem Analysis ===
This problem relates to optimal rod placement to minimize
the convex hull perimeter or area. Each rod can be in one
of two orientations (0° or 90°), creating 2^N configurations.

For large N, this becomes a combinatorial optimization
problem solvable via dynamic programming or greedy
algorithms on the Manhattan/wrapping metrics.

PE answer: 0.1091523673
